    "aboutTraceon": "About Traceon",
    "aboutIntro1": "<b>Traceon</b> is an <b>investigation and intelligence platform</b> built to support complex research workflows involving <b>people, organizations, infrastructure, and online activity</b>.",
    "aboutIntro2": "Whether you're conducting <b>cyber investigations</b>, mapping out <b>fraud networks</b>, or gathering intelligence for <b>threat assessments</b>, Traceon helps you collect, visualize, and understand fragmented data points in a structured and interactive way.",
    "whatTraceonDoes": "What Traceon Does",
    "doesItem1": "<b>Connects scattered data</b> — emails, domains, social accounts, IPs, phone numbers, addresses, and more — into a single <b>investigative graph</b>.",
    "doesItem2": "Offers <b>visual enrichers</b> to pivot from one entity to related ones: find <b>connected individuals</b>, discover <b>infrastructure</b>, uncover <b>aliases</b>.",
    "doesItem3": "<b>Tracks and saves investigation states</b> over time, letting you explore multiple hypotheses or revisit older threads without losing context.",
    "doesItem4": "Supports <b>live data enrichment</b> from custom or built-in enrichers, giving you <b>actionable insights</b> as you explore.",
    "whyUseTraceon": "Why Use Traceon?",
    "whyItem1": "Built for <b>speed and clarity</b> — fast graph rendering, clean UI, responsive enrichers.",
    "whyItem2": "<b>Flexible graph model</b> that mirrors how investigators think — not just tables and tags, but <b>relationships</b>.",
    "whyItem3": "Ideal for <b>solo analysts and teams</b> that need to move fast, explore freely, and make sense of <b>partial or messy data</b>.",
    "useCases": "Use Cases",
    "useCase1": "Mapping <b>digital infrastructure</b> of individuals or organizations",
    "useCase2": "Investigating <b>online fraud schemes</b> or <b>fake identities</b>",
    "useCase3": "Uncovering <b>links between actors</b> across platforms",
    "useCase4": "Visualizing the reach of <b>leaked or exposed data</b>",
    "useCase5": "Tracking <b>threat actor behavior</b> across social and technical surfaces",
    "aboutOutro": "Traceon is designed for <b>professionals</b> who need <b>full control</b> over their investigation logic, from how data is structured to how relationships are interpreted. It's not just a tool — it's a <b>flexible workspace</b> for building intelligence."
